@startuml
' Figure 6.1 -- What crosses the gap between two sessions.
' Anything written where the harness can read it back survives. Everything
' held in the conversation or in the programmer's head does not, and nothing
' in the loop reports the loss.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderThickness 1
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  FontColor black
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor white
  BorderColor black
  FontColor black
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor black
  BackgroundColor white
  FontColor black
}

package "Session 1" as S1 {
  rectangle "Conversation\ncorrections, explanations,\nthe reasoning behind them" as C1
  rectangle "Written down\nspec, constitution, issue,\ncommitted code" as W1 #lightgray
}

package "Session 2" as S2 {
  rectangle "Context assembled\nby the harness" as CTX #lightgray
  rectangle "Absent\nand not reported as absent" as GONE
}

rectangle "  T H E   G A P  \nprocess ends; model retains nothing" as GAP

C1 -down-> GAP
W1 -down-> GAP

GAP -down-> CTX : the harness reads\nthese back
GAP -down-> GONE : everything else

note right of GONE
  The loop does not
  notice the difference.
  It interpolates instead.
end note

@enduml
